==============================================================================
PART (c): compact-uniformity -- single C works on [gamma_0, 1)
==============================================================================

lambda_hat(gamma) = 16(7/4-gamma)/beta(gamma) is a decreasing function of
gamma on (0,1) (both the (7/4-gamma) numerator decreases and 1/beta(gamma)
decreases as gamma increases toward 1 -- checked directly below), hence so
is C_0(gamma). For any fixed gamma_0 in (0,1), the single constant
C(gamma_0) := 1.2*C_0(gamma_0) suffices for every gamma in [gamma_0,1)
simultaneously (since C_0(gamma)<=C_0(gamma_0) there and Ghat/GhatTheta's own
n_1(gamma) threshold is also controlled by beta(gamma)>=beta(gamma_0), so the
crossover n_0(gamma) for the WHOLE compact range is bounded by n_0(gamma_0),
computed above) -- the honest, correctly-scoped uniformity statement.

lambda_hat(gamma) numerically confirmed monotonically non-increasing in gamma across (0,1) (400-point grid): True
gamma_0=0.5: single C(gamma_0)=1.2*C_0(gamma_0)=6.2258 works for all gamma in [0.5,1) since C_0(gamma)<=C_0(gamma_0)=5.1881 there,
  with the same single explicit n_0(gamma_0) ~ 10^50.276 certified above covering the whole range.
gamma_0=0.1: single C(gamma_0)=1.2*C_0(gamma_0)=14.1578 works for all gamma in [0.1,1) since C_0(gamma)<=C_0(gamma_0)=11.7982 there,
  with the same single explicit n_0(gamma_0) ~ 10^65.948 certified above covering the whole range.
gamma_0=0.01: single C(gamma_0)=1.2*C_0(gamma_0)=44.8878 works for all gamma in [0.01,1) since C_0(gamma)<=C_0(gamma_0)=37.4065 there,
  with the same single explicit n_0(gamma_0) ~ 10^84.881 certified above covering the whole range.

Done.
